> 
> 
> > Hey, this has indeed solved the issue of saving the scene. But now if I try to load the same scene back into the game I receive the following error.
> > `Feb 28 22:54:16.854 WARN bevy_asset::asset_server: encountered an error while loading an asset: No registration found for std::collections::hash::set::HashSet<alloc::string::String, ahash::random_state::RandomState>`
> 
> You have to register the types of your components in your app builder for them to be usable in a scene.
> For example, a lot of basic types are registered in `bevy_reflect`:
> 
> https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/blob/3319195f9036e9ee301545632b98f1090a3ba3b0/crates/bevy_reflect/src/impls/bevy_app.rs#L11-L15
> 
> Types used for render are registered in `bevy_render`
> 
> https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/blob/89a41bc62843be5f92b4b978f6d801af4de14a2d/crates/bevy_render/src/lib.rs#L129-L134
> 
> and so on...
> 
> Is this from only default components of Bevy, or are you adding a custom component that is using a `HashSet`?

This issue came up while trying to load the saved scn.ron scene with 0 custom types. This is the scene setup code 

```
fn scene_setup(
    commands: &mut Commands,
    mut meshes: ResMut<Assets<Mesh>>,
    mut materials: ResMut<Assets<StandardMaterial>>,
) {
    commands
        .spawn(PbrBundle {
            mesh: meshes.add(Mesh::from(shape::Cube { size: 1.0 })),
            material: materials.add(Color::rgb(1.0, 0.0, 0.0).into()),
            ..Default::default()
        })
        .with(Transform::from_xyz(0.0, 8.0, 0.0))
        .with_children(|parent| {
            parent.spawn(PerspectiveCameraBundle {
                transform: Transform::from_xyz(0.0, 0.0, 0.0),
                ..Default::default()
            });
        });

    commands
        .spawn(PbrBundle {
            mesh: meshes.add(Mesh::from(shape::Cube { size: 1.0 })),
            material: materials.add(Color::rgb(0.8, 0.7, 0.6).into()),
            ..Default::default()
        })
        .with(Transform::from_xyz(0.0, 100.0, 0.0));

    commands.spawn(LightBundle {
        transform: Transform::from_xyz(4.0, 8.0, 4.0),
        ..Default::default()
    });
}
```

it produces this .scn.ron structure https://gist.github.com/Dmajster/1388706cee3617648b6c62bc5888b62d

the field it's complaining about is part of bevy_render::pipeline::render_pipelines::RenderPipelines

@mockersf It sounds like a good idea to me.
- ✅ Registered `HashSet<String>` in `bevy_core`
- ❌ Attempting to register `<HashMap<Handle<Texture>, usize>>` crashes with an error about the trait `GetTypeRegistration` not being implemented for it. It looks like that trait is implemented as part of a `#[reflect(...)]` or a `#[reflect_value(...)]`, so I _think_ this cannot be registered because `<HashMap<Handle<Texture>, usize>>` is not being reflected in the first place.
